neo-stopmotion (1.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix video playback on NEO One: force the GStreamer media backend (the
    PyQt6 wheel's ffmpeg backend links against libav*.so.58 while Debian 12
    ships ffmpeg 5.x, so Qt loaded no backend at all and the film stayed
    black), and depend on libgstreamer-plugins-bad1.0-0 which Qt's GStreamer
    plugin needs for libgstphotography.
  * SuccessPage now loops the film with a 5 second rest between plays instead
    of MediaPlayer.Infinite, which wedged after a few loops on this hardware.
  * EXPORT ends the film exactly once: pressing Enter (or the red ThingBot
    button) again no longer re-renders a finished film or starts a second
    ffmpeg pipeline.

 -- Maker Việt <everwellmax@gmail.com>  Wed, 19 Aug 2026 22:00:00 +0700

neo-stopmotion (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging.
  * Architecture-independent package; PyQt6, OpenCV, numpy, ffmpeg and
    the Qt6 QML runtime are pulled from apt (never built via pip),
    matching the ARM install strategy of scripts/install_on_neo.sh.

 -- Maker Việt <everwellmax@gmail.com>  Sun, 12 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0700
